    "System.CreatedDate": "2026-09-03T18:15:53.61Z",
    "System.Description": "<h2>What needs to be done </h2> <p>Add Date Range and Formula Range links to the web Report Designer. A Date Range link creates the report-period labels used by periodic content, including labels such as Total and the run years, and remains usable by other links after the template is saved and reopened. </p> <p>A Formula Range link uses the first periodic formula as its source and expands that formula across the linked range in the template's direction using the corresponding fill behavior. Both range types must preserve their workbook ranges and link metadata through save, reopen, and report generation. </p><hr><h2>Existing description and implementation details </h2><div><b>Sequencing note:</b> None for Date Range. Formula Range is blocked  see open question below. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Requirements</b> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Conceptual distinction from variable linking</b> </div><div>Ranges (Date Range, Formula Range) add content to the report rather than mapping a single variable's value into a cell  this is distinct from the variable linking mechanism covered in 1869322. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Date Range link</b> </div><div>Author can create a Date Range link (WPF: Ranges &gt; Date Range &gt; Link), producing a range of row/column labels tied to the report run period (e.g. Total/2020/2021 rows generated from a linked range). Variable Type for a Date Range link is &quot;Periodic Date&quot;. Confirmed working example: Range =Sheet1!$C$24:$C$26 produces Total/2020/2021 labels referenced by Periodic Links elsewhere in the template. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Formula Range link  open question, functionality not yet understood</b> </div><div>Web Report Designer must also support Formula Range links (WPF: Ranges &gt; Formula Range &gt; Link), producing &lt;SUMMARY&gt;, &lt;FIRST VALUE&gt;, and &lt;SECOND VALUE&gt; placeholders. It is unclear whether Formula Range ties to a spreadsheet formula's output, an auto-derived calculation over a range (e.g. min/max or start/end of a series), or something else. Neither Marg nor Claude could determine this from UAT inspection. Needs investigation with engineering before AC can be written for this portion. </div>",
